=================== FORMS-SETUP.md ===================
# Forms — built into the layout

**Yes, the forms can live inside the elements and route themselves.**

I was wrong earlier when I said they couldn't. Custom elements can't call Velo *backend modules* — but they **can** fetch a **Velo HTTP Function**, which is a real URL on your own site. Same origin, no auth, no page code.

One element, three forms, one backend file.

---

## How it works

```
arise-form element  →  POST /_functions/ariseForm  →  http-functions.js
                                                         ├── saves to Form Submissions (CMS)
                                                         └── emails the right address
```

Which form appears is set by an attribute in the Editor:

| Page | Attribute | Fields | Goes to |
|---|---|---|---|
| Contact | `data-form="contact"` | Name, Email, Phone, Subject, Message | arisenow.church@gmail.com |
| Serve | `data-form="serve"` | Name, Email, Phone, Position, Notes | arisenow.church@gmail.com |
| Anywhere | `data-form="prayer"` | Name, Email, Prayer Request | arisechurchprayer@gmail.com |

The **Serve** form's Position dropdown is your five real roles: Children's Department, Outreach, Media/Social Media, Edge/X Edge, Maintenance.

---

## 1. Backend — `backend/http-functions.js`

Velo sidebar → **Backend** → the file must be named exactly `http-functions.js`.

```javascript
import { ok, badRequest, serverError } from 'wix-http-functions';
import wixData from 'wix-data';
import { triggeredEmails } from 'wix-crm-backend';

// Where each form goes. Change these addresses if routing changes.
const ROUTES = {
  contact: 'arisenow.church@gmail.com',
  serve:   'arisenow.church@gmail.com',
  prayer:  'arisechurchprayer@gmail.com'
};

function clean(v, max) {
  return String(v == null ? '' : v).trim().slice(0, max || 2000);
}

export async function post_ariseForm(request) {
  try {
    const body = await request.body.json();

    const formType = clean(body.formType, 40).toLowerCase();
    if (!ROUTES[formType]) return badRequest({ body: { error: 'unknown form' } });

    const name    = clean(body.name, 120);
    const email   = clean(body.email, 200);
    const message = clean(body.message, 4000);

    if (!name || !email) return badRequest({ body: { error: 'name and email required' } });
    if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) {
      return badRequest({ body: { error: 'invalid email' } });
    }

    const record = {
      formType,
      name,
      email,
      phone:    clean(body.phone, 60),
      subject:  clean(body.subject, 200),
      position: clean(body.position, 120),
      message,
      handled:  false
    };

    // 1. Always store it — nothing is lost even if email fails.
    await wixData.insert('FormSubmissions', record, { suppressAuth: true });

    // 2. Notify. Requires a triggered email named "formSubmission" — see below.
    try {
      await triggeredEmails.emailContact('formSubmission', ROUTES[formType], {
        variables: {
          formType, name, email,
          phone: record.phone || '-',
          subject: record.subject || '-',
          position: record.position || '-',
          message: message || '-'
        }
      });
    } catch (mailErr) {
      console.error('Form email failed (submission still saved):', mailErr);
    }

    return ok({ body: { ok: true } });

  } catch (err) {
    console.error('ariseForm failed:', err);
    return serverError({ body: { error: 'server error' } });
  }
}
```

---

## 2. The element

Paste `arise-form.js` into `public/custom-elements/`.

Then on each page: **Add → Embed Code → Custom Element → Choose Source → Velo file → `arise-form.js`**, tag name **`arise-form`**.

**Then set the attribute.** In the element's settings there's a place to add custom attributes:

```
name:   data-form
value:  contact        (or serve, or prayer)
```

Stretch it full width. That's the whole setup — same element on every page, different attribute.

---

## 3. Email notifications — one dashboard step

The backend saves every submission to the CMS regardless. For email on top:

**Dashboard → Automations → New Automation**
- Trigger: **Velo code trigger** (or Triggered Email)
- Name the trigger exactly: **`formSubmission`**
- Action: **Send an email**
- Available variables: `formType` `name` `email` `phone` `subject` `position` `message`

**If you skip this**, submissions still save — you'd just check the CMS instead of your inbox. Nothing is lost either way.

---

## Where submissions live

**CMS → Form Submissions.** Every entry has the form type, all fields, and a `handled` checkbox so you can track what's been answered.

That's better than Wix Forms in one respect: **you own the data**, and it's queryable.

---

## What the visitor sees

Required fields marked in red. Inline validation before anything is sent — empty required fields and malformed emails are caught in the browser. The email format is checked again on the server, so it can't be bypassed.

On success, the form is replaced by a thank-you panel. On failure, an error appears **with your email address as a fallback**, so a broken form never means a lost visitor.

---

## Two honest notes

**Test on the published site.** `/_functions/` URLs don't resolve in Preview.

**This replaces the Wix form on Contact.** Once it's working, remove the old one — otherwise you have two forms doing the same job and submissions split between two places.

=================== EVENTS-SETUP.md ===================
# Events — automatic from Wix Events

Two files. Once they're in, **every event you create in Wix Events appears on the page by itself** — with its own uploaded image, the right button, and a link to its own registration page.

Nothing to edit in code when you add an event.

---

## What the button says

Read straight from each event's registration settings:

| Event setup | Button |
|---|---|
| RSVP, open | **RSVP** |
| Ticketed, open | **Get Tickets** |
| Sold out | **Sold Out** — greyed, not clickable |
| Closed or ended | **View Event** |
| External registration | **Register** |
| No registration | **View Event** |

---

## 1. Backend — `backend/events.jsw`

```javascript
import { events } from 'wix-events.v2';
import { elevate } from 'wix-auth';

const elevatedQuery = elevate(events.queryEvents);

function ctaFor(ev) {
  const reg = ev.registration || {};
  const type = reg.type;
  const status = reg.status || '';

  if (reg.registrationDisabled) return { cta: 'View Event', ctaEnabled: true };

  if (type === 'TICKETING') {
    if (reg.tickets && reg.tickets.soldOut) return { cta: 'Sold Out', ctaEnabled: false };
    if (status.indexOf('OPEN') === 0) return { cta: 'Get Tickets', ctaEnabled: true };
    return { cta: 'View Event', ctaEnabled: true };
  }
  if (type === 'RSVP') {
    if (status === 'OPEN_RSVP_WAITLIST') return { cta: 'Join Waitlist', ctaEnabled: true };
    if (status.indexOf('OPEN') === 0) return { cta: 'RSVP', ctaEnabled: true };
    return { cta: 'View Event', ctaEnabled: true };
  }
  if (type === 'EXTERNAL') return { cta: 'Register', ctaEnabled: true };
  return { cta: 'View Event', ctaEnabled: true };
}

function shape(ev) {
  const dt = ev.dateAndTimeSettings || {};
  const f  = dt.formatted || {};
  const start = dt.startDate ? new Date(dt.startDate) : null;
  const loc = ev.location || {};
  const addr = (loc.address && loc.address.formatted) || '';

  return Object.assign({
    id: ev._id || ev.id,
    title: ev.title || '',
    shortDescription: ev.shortDescription || '',
    image: (ev.mainImage && (ev.mainImage.url || ev.mainImage)) || '',
    dateLine: f.dateAndTime || '',
    startDate: f.startDate || '',
    startMonth: start ? start.toLocaleString('en-US', { month: 'short' }) : '',
    startDay: start ? String(start.getDate()) : '',
    location: addr || loc.name || '',
    url: (ev.eventPageUrl && ev.eventPageUrl.path) || ''
  }, ctaFor(ev));
}

/**
 * Upcoming events (soonest first) and past events (most recent first).
 */
export async function getEvents() {
  try {
    const res = await elevatedQuery({ fields: ['DETAILS', 'TEXTS', 'REGISTRATION', 'URLS'] })
      .ne('status', 'CANCELED')
      .limit(50)
      .find();

    const all = (res.items || []).map(shape);
    const raw = res.items || [];

    const upcoming = [], past = [];
    raw.forEach((ev, i) => {
      const s = all[i];
      if (!s.url) return;
      if (ev.status === 'UPCOMING' || ev.status === 'STARTED') upcoming.push(s);
      else if (ev.status === 'ENDED') past.push(s);
    });

    upcoming.sort((a, b) => (a.dateLine > b.dateLine ? 1 : -1));
    past.reverse();

    return { upcoming, past: past.slice(0, 8) };
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('getEvents failed:', err);
    return { upcoming: [], past: [] };
  }
}
```

---

## 2. Events page code

```javascript
import { getEvents } from 'backend/events.jsw';

// Right-click the custom element -> View Properties to confirm this ID.
const EL = '#customElement1';

$w.onReady(async () => {
  if (!$w(EL).length) {
    console.warn('Events: custom element ' + EL + ' not found.');
    return;
  }

  try {
    const data = await getEvents();
    if (data && (data.upcoming.length || data.past.length)) {
      $w(EL).setAttribute('data-events', JSON.stringify(data));
      console.log('Events loaded:', data.upcoming.length, 'upcoming,', data.past.length, 'past');
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Events load failed:', err);
    // element keeps its built-in fallback
  }
});
```

---

## What the page becomes

**Featured** — your next upcoming event, using its own uploaded poster, with the date block, time, location, and the correct button.

**Also Coming Up** — every other upcoming event as a card.

**Previous Events** — your past events with their real images, most recent first, capped at eight. That section was an empty placeholder before.

You have **13 events** in Wix Events right now, so the past grid fills immediately.

---

## Adding a new event

Create it in Wix Events as normal. Nothing else. The site picks up its image, dates, location, registration type and link on the next page load.

**The image is whatever you upload as the event's main image** — so make it a good one. It's the biggest thing on the page.

---

## If the backend import fails

Some sites expose the events module differently. If `wix-events.v2` errors, try:

```javascript
import { events } from 'wix-events-backend';
```

and drop the `elevate` wrapper — `queryEvents` on that module runs with site permissions already.

Everything else stays the same. Tell me which one your site accepts and I'll lock the file to it.

=================== SERMONS-LIVE-SETUP.md ===================
# Sermons — Automatic Live Stream Detection

Two files. Once these are in, the featured player switches to your live stream on its own — Sunday mornings, Monday Glory Nights, and any other time you go live.

**No API key. No cost. Nothing to remember on a Sunday.**

---

## What happens

| State | Player shows | Badge |
|---|---|---|
| **You're streaming** | The live stream | **LIVE NOW** — red, pulsing dot |
| Not streaming | Your most recent livestream | **Latest Service** |

The page also **re-checks every 60 seconds**. So if a visitor opens the page five minutes before service and you start streaming, it switches over for them without a refresh.

---

## 1. Backend — `backend/youtube.jsw`

Velo sidebar → **Backend** → new file named exactly `youtube.jsw`.

```javascript
import { fetch } from 'wix-fetch';

const CHANNEL_ID = 'UCGS9j7B_prcJkbTNgzlGrKg';

// Short cache so a busy Sunday doesn't hammer YouTube.
let cache = { value: null, at: 0 };
const CACHE_MS = 45000;

/**
 * Returns the videoId of the current live stream, or null when not streaming.
 * Reads YouTube's public /live page — no API key needed.
 */
export async function getLiveVideoId() {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - cache.at < CACHE_MS) return cache.value;

  let result = null;

  try {
    const res = await fetch(
      `https://www.youtube.com/channel/${CHANNEL_ID}/live`,
      { method: 'get', headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible)' } }
    );

    if (res.ok) {
      const html = await res.text();

      // Signal 1 — when live, the canonical link is a watch URL.
      const canonical = html.match(/<link rel="canonical" href="([^"]+)"/);
      if (canonical && canonical[1].includes('/watch?v=')) {
        const id = canonical[1].split('/watch?v=')[1].split('&')[0];
        if (/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}$/.test(id)) result = id;
      }

      // Signal 2 — fallback if the canonical is missing.
      if (!result && html.includes('"isLive":true')) {
        const vid = html.match(/"videoId":"([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})"/);
        if (vid) result = vid[1];
      }
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Live check failed:', err);
    result = null;           // fail quiet — player keeps the latest stream
  }

  cache = { value: result, at: now };
  return result;
}
```

---

## 2. Past Sermons page code

Pages → **Past Sermons** → ⋮ → Page Code.

```javascript
import { getLiveVideoId } from 'backend/youtube.jsw';

// Rename this if your element's ID differs.
// Right-click the custom element -> View Properties to check.
const ELEMENT_ID = '#customElement1';

$w.onReady(() => {
  if (!$w(ELEMENT_ID).length) {
    console.warn('Sermons: custom element ' + ELEMENT_ID + ' not found.');
    return;
  }

  let current = null;

  async function check() {
    try {
      const liveId = await getLiveVideoId();
      if (liveId === current) return;      // nothing changed
      current = liveId;

      if (liveId) {
        $w(ELEMENT_ID).setAttribute('data-live-video', liveId);
        console.log('Live stream detected:', liveId);
      } else {
        $w(ELEMENT_ID).setAttribute('data-live-video', '');
      }
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Live check failed:', err);
    }
  }

  check();                        // on load
  setInterval(check, 60000);      // and every 60 seconds after
});
```

**Check the element's ID before you paste.** Right-click the custom element → View Properties. Wix usually names it `#customElement1`, but not always — and a wrong ID here fails silently.

---

## How the detection works

YouTube's `/live` URL gives it away without any API:

- **Streaming** → its canonical link points at a `watch?v=` URL
- **Not streaming** → it points back at the channel

I tested this against your channel. It correctly reported not-live, and returned the channel canonical exactly as expected.

There's a second check on `"isLive":true` in case the canonical is ever missing.

---

## The featured playlist

Separately from live detection, the player's default is your **live streams playlist**:

| Prefix | Contains |
|---|---|
| `UU` | All uploads, Shorts included |
| `UULF` | Long-form only |
| **`UULV`** | **Live streams only** ← the player uses this |
| `UUSH` | Shorts only |

```
Channel:      UCGS9j7B_prcJkbTNgzlGrKg
Live streams: UULVGS9j7B_prcJkbTNgzlGrKg
```

Verified — its first entry matches the newest video on your `/streams` tab.

---

## Testing it

**Best test is a real one.** Next time you go live, open the Sermons page and watch the badge turn red.

**Before then**, open the browser console on the published page. You should see the check running with no errors. When live, it logs `Live stream detected: <videoId>`.

---

## Honest caveat

This reads YouTube's public HTML rather than an official API. It works today and needs no key, but YouTube could change their markup without warning.

**If that ever happens, the page doesn't break** — it falls back to showing your most recent livestream, which during a service is usually that same stream anyway. You'd lose the LIVE badge, not the video.

If you'd rather have something contract-backed, the official YouTube Data API does this properly with a free key. Say the word and I'll write that version instead.

=================== SERMONS-SERIES-AUTO.md ===================
# Sermons — Automatic Series Detection

The site reads your YouTube playlists and uses the most recent one as the Current Series band.

**The habit:** when a series starts, make a YouTube playlist named after it and add the messages as you go. That's useful on YouTube anyway — and it's how the website finds out.

---

## How it decides — your own naming convention

You have twelve playlists, and four already say **"Series"** in the name:

- Fruit of the Spirit **(Series)**
- No Killer, No King **(Series)**
- The Believers Authority **(Series)**
- Sermon **Series**: This Is Us (2019)

So that's the rule: **a playlist is the current series if its name contains "series".**

Opt-in, unambiguous, nothing to maintain — and it's already how you name them. Glory Nights, Sunday Sermons, Conferences & Special Events and the rest are simply never candidates.

An ignore list stays as a backstop in case an evergreen playlist ever gets an awkward name:

```javascript
const IGNORE = ['sunday sermons', 'lead network', 'iserve september',
                'glory nights | arise church', 'conferences & special events',
                'apostle bryant sanders — messages'];
```

> **Name your series playlists with "(Series)".** One word, and the website updates itself.

---

## Order of precedence

1. **Manual override** — if `seriesActive` is ticked in **CMS → Site Settings**, that wins. Always.
2. **Auto-detect** — otherwise, the newest playlist not on the ignore list.
3. **Nothing** — if neither applies, the band hides itself.

So you can always overrule it, and between series the band simply disappears.

---

## 1. Backend — add to `backend/youtube.jsw`

```javascript
/* ---- Current series, read from the channel's playlists ---------------- */

const IGNORE = ['sunday sermons', 'lead network', 'iserve september'];

let seriesCache = { value: null, at: 0 };
const SERIES_CACHE_MS = 600000;   // 10 minutes

/**
 * Returns { title, url } for the newest playlist that isn't on the ignore
 * list, or null. Playlists appear newest-first on the channel's tab.
 */
export async function getCurrentSeries() {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - seriesCache.at < SERIES_CACHE_MS) return seriesCache.value;

  let result = null;

  try {
    const res = await fetch(
      `https://www.youtube.com/channel/${CHANNEL_ID}/playlists`,
      { method: 'get', headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible)' } }
    );

    if (res.ok) {
      const html = await res.text();
      const seen = new Set();

      // NOTE: playlist IDs come in two lengths — 13 and 34 characters.
      // Matching {16,} silently misses most of them.
      const re = /"playlistId":"(PL[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,})"/g;
      let m;
      while ((m = re.exec(html)) !== null) {
        const pid = m[1];
        if (seen.has(pid)) continue;
        seen.add(pid);

        // title sits near the id in the same block
        const seg = html.slice(m.index, m.index + 3000);
        const t = seg.match(/"title":\{"runs":\[\{"text":"([^"]{2,90})"/) ||
                  seg.match(/"title":\{"simpleText":"([^"]{2,90})"/);
        if (!t) continue;

        const title = t[1].trim();
        const lower = title.toLowerCase();

        if (IGNORE.includes(lower)) continue;
        if (!lower.includes('series')) continue;   // opt-in by name

        result = {
          // drop a trailing "(Series)" so the heading reads cleanly
          title: title.replace(/\s*\(series\)\s*$/i, '').trim(),
          url: `https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=${pid}`
        };
        break;                       // first non-ignored = newest
      }
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Series lookup failed:', err);
    result = null;
  }

  seriesCache = { value: result, at: now };
  return result;
}
```

---

## 2. Past Sermons page code — replace the whole file

```javascript
import wixData from 'wix-data';
import { getLiveVideoId, getCurrentSeries } from 'backend/youtube.jsw';

// Right-click the custom element -> View Properties to confirm this ID.
const EL = '#customElement1';

$w.onReady(async () => {
  if (!$w(EL).length) {
    console.warn('Sermons: custom element ' + EL + ' not found.');
    return;
  }

  // ---- Series band ------------------------------------------------------
  try {
    let title = null, line = null, link = null, label = null;

    // 1. Manual override from the CMS always wins
    const { items } = await wixData.query('SiteSettings')
      .eq('settingKey', 'sermonSeries')
      .limit(1)
      .find();

    const s = items[0];
    if (s && s.seriesActive && s.seriesTitle) {
      title = s.seriesTitle;
      line  = s.seriesLine  || null;
      link  = s.seriesLink  || null;
      label = s.seriesButton || null;
    } else {
      // 2. Otherwise auto-detect from YouTube playlists
      const auto = await getCurrentSeries();
      if (auto) {
        title = auto.title;
        link  = auto.url;
        label = 'Watch the Series';
      }
    }

    if (title) {
      $w(EL).setAttribute('data-series-active', 'true');
      $w(EL).setAttribute('data-series-title', title);
      $w(EL).setAttribute('data-series-line', line || '');
      if (link)  $w(EL).setAttribute('data-series-link', link);
      if (label) $w(EL).setAttribute('data-series-button', label);
      console.log('Series band:', title);
    } else {
      $w(EL).setAttribute('data-series-active', 'false');   // hides the band
      console.log('Series band: none active, hidden');
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Series lookup failed:', err);
  }

  // ---- Live stream detection -------------------------------------------
  let current = null;

  async function checkLive() {
    try {
      const liveId = await getLiveVideoId();
      if (liveId === current) return;
      current = liveId;
      $w(EL).setAttribute('data-live-video', liveId || '');
      if (liveId) console.log('Live stream detected:', liveId);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Live check failed:', err);
    }
  }

  checkLive();
  setInterval(checkLive, 60000);
});
```

---

## Using it day to day

**New series starts** — make the playlist with **"(Series)"** in the name. The site picks it up within ten minutes.

**Series ends, nothing new** — rename the playlist to drop "Series", or set the CMS override. Band disappears.

**Want to override** — tick `seriesActive` in CMS → Site Settings and set the title. Manual always beats automatic.

**Playlist name is the heading**, so name it the way you want it read on the site. "The Kingdom Culture of Giving" reads better than "kingdom giving series 2026".

---

## Two honest caveats

**Playlist name = series name.** Whatever you type on YouTube appears on the site, "(Series)" included — so write it the way you want it read. The code strips a trailing "(Series)" for you, but nothing else.

**This reads YouTube's public HTML**, not an official API. It works today, needs no key, and is cached for ten minutes. If YouTube changes their markup, detection stops and the band falls back to your CMS setting — or hides. **It degrades quietly; it doesn't break the page.**

If you'd rather have something contract-backed, the official YouTube Data API does playlists properly with a free key. Say the word.

