  { key: 'lens:backend', prompt: 'Audit every backend and page-code snippet embedded in the docs (there are NO backend files in the zips; the code exists only inside the markdown). Sources under ' + ROOT + '/files: FORMS-SETUP.md, CONNECT-SETUP.md, EVENTS-SETUP.md, CMS-SETUP.md, CREATIVES-SETUP.md, SERVE-SETUP.md, HOME-VIDEO-SETUP.md, PAGECONTENT-SETUP.md, ALEXANDRIA-SETUP.md, CLASSES-SETUP.md, GALLERY-SETUP.md, SERMONS-LIVE-SETUP.md, SERMONS-SERIES-AUTO.md, ALL-PAGE-CODE.md, VELO-CMS-GUIDE.md; and ' + ROOT + '/files2/ARISE-HANDOFF.md section 5. ' + COMMON + ' For each snippet check: Velo API misuse (for example wix-crm-backend triggeredEmails.emailContact takes (emailId, contactId, options) -- a raw email address is not a contactId; wix-events.v2 queryEvents shape, fields and status enums; wix-auth elevate usage; webMethod/Permissions/auth imports present in every file that uses them; is imgUrl, referenced by PAGECONTENT-SETUP and ALEXANDRIA-SETUP, defined in ANY doc?; is "auth" imported in CLASSES-SETUP getPrograms?); conflicting versions of the same backend file across docs (http-functions.js ROUTES vs ALLOWED vs the handoff version; getPageContent returning {text,image} vs string|{text,imageUrl}); which data-content shape do the elements ACTUALLY accept -- read applyContent() in ' + FIXED + '/arise-home.js and T()/IMG() in ' + FIXED + '/arise-alexandria.js and say which doc version is compatible with which element; the email regex backslash issue (\\\\s vs \\s) in every copy; page-code element-ID assumptions; error handling; anything the handoff says is still pending (ALLOWED list). Also verify every backend export a page-code snippet imports exists in some doc, and that each page-code snippet sets exactly the attribute names the target element observes (grep observedAttributes). Mark anything you are unsure about as medium/low confidence inside the evidence text.' },
